# Do it yourself — always

Owner order: **делай все сам всегда**.

1. Prefer API/CLI/scripts/Edge/Playwright/`gsudo` — not “open Settings and click…”.
2. No manual checklists when you can run the action.
3. Human gate only (UAC/OAuth/passkey): open prompt/URL, wait/poll, finish remaining work (`wait-for-user-login` when relevant).
4. Defender/IDE/MCP/plugins: automate; re-enable Defender after temp off.
5. Customize/MCP cleanup: lean tools (CF MCPs, Playwright, GitHub, Figma/Notion/Linear). Do not reinstall unused erroring plugins (e.g. Datadog).
6. Images/screenshots: binary media like `*.png`/`*.jpg` can be read normally if needed; visual analysis still uses Playwright/browser when model supports image input, otherwise use browser screenshot/snapshot.
7. For local image analysis, run `node tools/image-server.mjs <folder> <port>` to serve files, navigate Playwright to `http://127.0.0.1:<port>/<filename>`, then screenshot.

Image-analysis protocol:
- Remote URL → navigate → screenshot.
- Project-local file in web root → `http://localhost:5502/<relative-path>` → screenshot.
- Arbitrary local file → `node tools/image-server.mjs <file-dir> 8767` → `http://127.0.0.1:8767/<file>` → screenshot.
- Default screenshots folder → `C:\Users\snaip\Pictures\Screenshots` → `node tools/image-server.mjs "C:\Users\snaip\Pictures\Screenshots" 8768` → `http://127.0.0.1:8768/<file>` → screenshot.
